cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Physics Surrogate Benchmarks"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "El Moutaouakil"
    given-names: "Tarik"
    email: "elmoutaouakiltarik-web@users.noreply.github.com"
    website: "https://github.com/elmoutaouakiltarik-web"
repository-code: "https://github.com/elmoutaouakiltarik-web/physics-surrogate-benchmarks"
url: "https://github.com/elmoutaouakiltarik-web/physics-surrogate-benchmarks"
abstract: >-
  Small PyTorch implementations of two surrogate-model families - a physics-informed
  neural network for the 1D viscous Burgers equation and a Fourier neural operator for
  the periodic heat operator - each scored against a closed-form reference solution so
  that the reported error is the error of the model alone. The repository also ships
  the published Ghia, Ghia & Shin (1982) lid-driven-cavity profiles as benchmark data,
  a divergence-free manufactured solution for metric verification, and tests that keep
  the committed weights, result files and README numbers in agreement.
keywords:
  - surrogate-modeling
  - physics-informed-neural-networks
  - fourier-neural-operator
  - cfd
  - computational-fluid-dynamics
  - verification-and-validation
  - benchmark
  - pytorch
